I played for a month or two in high school, but never seriously --
didn't read any spoilers, etc. Started playing seriously about two
months ago with a bunch of friends at MIT, finally pulled it off. This
was the first game I even completed Sokoban, let alone hit the quest
or Medusa, etc. I read nearly every page on the wiki, and had lots of
advice from experienced players.

Headed down to the mines first. Around level 5, my dog polymorph
trapped into a vampire lord. Having found a magic whistle, this was
hugely useful for a while, since I could just call in the vamp to deal
with anything that was getting too tough. Sac'd for Mjollnir, and
headed down. Got the "oR from Sokoban, stumbled on a shield of
reflection somewhere. Killed Medusa before the quest, and then killed
a gray dragon and enchanted his scales into GDSM.

Got the wand of wishing, wished for:
BoH
Speed boots
Ring of conflict
Two scrolls of genocide (h and L, they were the only things being
annoying in Gehennom)
Magic wand (for enchant armor, my AC was crap)

Pretty much everything was easy from that point, I just VALK SMASH'd
through everything. The one hairy moment was when I accidentally read
a scroll of destroy armor and killed my shield of reflection. I still
had the "oR, but this meant I couldn't wear any of the *three* "oLS
I'd found at that point. Luckily, Rodney spawned an Archon, who
dropped another one on the way out.

The planes were no problem; I used the Orb of Fate with no problems,
and pretty much just walked through.

I never learned about #enchance, so I apparently was wielding MJ the
whole way through without any hammer skill ...

